1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,819
Welcome to practicals twenty five and twenty six:

2
00:00:03,819 --> 00:00:07,248
feature engineering and selection in Python.

3
00:00:07,248 --> 00:00:15,432
This first video covers constructing features, interactions, polynomials and the curse of dimensionality.

4
00:00:16,232 --> 00:00:18,864
The main data is Online Shoppers:

5
00:00:18,864 --> 00:00:29,231
twelve thousand three hundred thirty sessions, eighteen columns, target Revenue, where fifteen and a half percent of sessions buy.

6
00:00:29,231 --> 00:00:32,660
The second worked example is Pima diabetes:

7
00:00:32,660 --> 00:00:39,518
seven hundred sixty eight patients, target outcome, with thirty five percent diabetic.

8
00:00:39,518 --> 00:00:40,475
Eight steps:

9
00:00:40,475 --> 00:00:46,456
construct, interact, polynomial, curse, filter, wrapper, embedded, compare.

10
00:00:46,456 --> 00:00:48,609
One rule for the whole lab:

11
00:00:48,609 --> 00:00:54,032
same model, same train and test split, and only the features change.

12
00:00:54,832 --> 00:00:56,830
Step zero is the imports:

13
00:00:56,830 --> 00:01:14,248
pandas and numpy, plotting libraries, the train test split, Standard Scaler and Polynomial Features, a pipeline, logistic regression and random forest, the feature selection tools, and the R O C A U C and F one scores.

14
00:01:15,048 --> 00:01:15,805
Step one:

15
00:01:15,805 --> 00:01:16,982
load the data.

16
00:01:16,982 --> 00:01:22,363
Convert weekend and revenue from true and false to one and zero.

17
00:01:22,363 --> 00:01:34,892
Only fifteen and a half percent buy, so we score models with R O C A U C, where zero point five is guessing and one is perfect, rather than accuracy.

18
00:01:34,892 --> 00:01:38,592
The ten behaviour columns form the baseline.

19
00:01:39,392 --> 00:01:40,125
Step two:

20
00:01:40,125 --> 00:01:43,220
one yardstick function for every test.

21
00:01:43,220 --> 00:01:58,370
The same seventy five twenty five split every time, stratified to keep fifteen and a half percent buyers in both parts, with a fixed random state, so every comparison in the lab is fair.

22
00:01:58,370 --> 00:02:06,515
A pipeline scales, fits logistic regression on train rows, and scores A U C on the unseen test rows.

23
00:02:06,515 --> 00:02:10,832
The baseline A U C is zero point eight five five two.

24
00:02:11,632 --> 00:02:14,079
Construct totals and ratios.

25
00:02:14,079 --> 00:02:17,488
Total pages adds the three page counts.

26
00:02:17,488 --> 00:02:20,984
Total duration adds the three durations.

27
00:02:20,984 --> 00:02:26,316
Average time per page divides, and product share divides too.

28
00:02:26,316 --> 00:02:37,066
Replace zero with missing avoids division by zero, and fill na zero sets empty sessions to zero, with no if or else needed.

29
00:02:37,066 --> 00:02:40,912
The table shows each feature's distribution.

30
00:02:41,712 --> 00:02:43,621
Construct zero-one flags:

31
00:02:43,621 --> 00:02:49,730
is returning visitor, has page value, and Q four season for October to December.

32
00:02:49,730 --> 00:02:58,436
About eighty six percent are returning, twenty two percent have page value, and forty three percent are in Q four.

33
00:02:58,436 --> 00:03:08,592
The group by shows the purchase rate is fifty six point three percent when has page value is one and only three point nine when zero.

34
00:03:09,392 --> 00:03:12,154
Construct a log transform and bands.

35
00:03:12,154 --> 00:03:19,212
Log one p of page values shrinks skewness from six point three eight to one point eight one.

36
00:03:19,212 --> 00:03:31,640
And qcut makes four duration bands with equal numbers of sessions; the purchase rate rises from four point three percent to twenty four percent and then flattens.

37
00:03:32,440 --> 00:03:35,085
Did the constructed features help?

38
00:03:35,085 --> 00:03:38,196
Compare the test A U C before and after:

39
00:03:38,196 --> 00:03:47,608
zero point eight five five two to zero point eight nine eight, a gain of zero point oh four three from eight new columns.

40
00:03:47,608 --> 00:03:58,264
The correlation chart shows log page values and has page value have the strongest absolute correlation with revenue, over zero point six.

41
00:03:59,064 --> 00:04:00,147
Interactions:

42
00:04:00,147 --> 00:04:02,397
check first, then multiply.

43
00:04:02,397 --> 00:04:11,812
The two-way table shows page value lifts new visitors to eighty six percent but returning ones only to fifty one:

44
00:04:11,812 --> 00:04:13,062
an interaction.

45
00:04:13,062 --> 00:04:20,560
We then create page value times returning, page value times Q four, and bounce times exit.

46
00:04:20,560 --> 00:04:26,976
A U C goes from zero point eight nine eight to zero point nine oh three nine.

47
00:04:27,776 --> 00:04:30,812
Polynomial features with scikit-learn.

48
00:04:30,812 --> 00:04:34,566
Three inputs at degree two become nine columns.

49
00:04:34,566 --> 00:04:41,596
The number of columns from ten inputs is C of ten plus degree, choose degree, minus one.

50
00:04:41,596 --> 00:04:54,218
At degree three, ten inputs give two eighty five columns, eighty five inputs give over one hundred nine thousand, and at degree five about forty four million.

51
00:04:54,218 --> 00:04:55,496
Columns explode.

52
00:04:56,296 --> 00:04:57,094
Curse one:

53
00:04:57,094 --> 00:04:59,807
the data uses less and less space.

54
00:04:59,807 --> 00:05:03,317
Cut each feature into four bins by quartile.

55
00:05:03,317 --> 00:05:12,891
With four features there are two fifty six possible cells and twelve thousand sessions occupy five hundred eighty seven.

56
00:05:12,891 --> 00:05:23,104
With ten features, there are over a million cells, and sessions touch only point two percent, about five rows per occupied cell.

57
00:05:23,904 --> 00:05:24,759
Curse two:

58
00:05:24,759 --> 00:05:27,922
more columns means more over-fitting.

59
00:05:27,922 --> 00:05:35,018
We train on only four hundred sessions and compare polynomial degrees one to three.

60
00:05:35,018 --> 00:05:37,069
Degree one, ten columns:

61
00:05:37,069 --> 00:05:42,199
train point eight eight three, test point eight seven eight.

62
00:05:42,199 --> 00:05:43,139
Degree two:

63
00:05:43,139 --> 00:05:47,755
train point nine two seven, test point eight oh three.

64
00:05:47,755 --> 00:05:51,688
Degree three, two hundred eighty five columns:

65
00:05:51,688 --> 00:05:56,817
train point nine nine six, test only point seven four three.

66
00:05:56,817 --> 00:05:59,040
The model memorised noise.

